what happens you know every time you annex land out and obviously it depends there's a big difference between a house versus a large development like say sweetgrass or a large business park or that sort of thing but ultimately what happens is you start stretching and expanding all of your services so water sewer lines have to expand of course fire service aspects and trash service has to expand the police department has to extend where it services the area and all those things come at a cost right to the city when you look at the house housing task force and the reason um i wanted to just briefly talk about this uh tonight um downtown um in particular but there's also many other areas in the city really present a lot of potential for infield development as it relates to downtown in particular there's a much higher upfront investment than you might see in terms of trying to remodel or revitalize some other areas for infill development however there's substantial square footage available there um

